      "value": "@{66c0f20001ed12a39619b034|full_name} so i found out that i was actually at first without the problem in steamvr beta the entire time but it wasnt titled as beta because i remembered off of a video that i would need to put myself on beta. when i had complications of steamvr... i noticed when i was on the beta tab that it showed a completely different version on the steamvr beta tab that i have no idea what that was about when vrchat got its new update. i later on as of today on 1am got everything fixed, i even got the steamvr app when you launch to airlink, even my own headset not recognizing itself... i accidently made it where the vr microphone wasnt used and had to use a headset. which gave it an error saying that there was no battery life when there is a bunch of battery life... when i launch vrchat i would randomly even off of my own phone i would disconnect from my wifi. i got everything back to normal the new ui is strange but i enjoyed the \"strange\" very much so. even though theres been thunderstorms roughly all this week and not much showered rain other than more than likely a couple of thunderstorms. though all this week i only had one incident of the power went out and it was just once and it quickly went right back on when it went out which was amazing. so when i got disconnected without storms i think it was due to vrchat couldnt handle itself i have no idea but turning on steamvr beta helped.",
